---
// Starlight ThemeProvider override. The docs have one scheme — the app's own
// look, dark chrome around a light page — so there is nothing to choose:
// Starlight's provider would read a stored preference or the OS setting and
// might land on its dark scheme, which the stylesheet no longer carries. This
// sets the light scheme inline, before paint, so there is no flash. The theme
// switcher is gone from the header (Header.astro), so the picker-syncing
// helper the default provider exposes isn't needed either.
---

<script is:inline>
	document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'light';
</script>
